Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: read the WAN MAC of the NX30 Pro from a provisioned source

The stock base reads the WAN MAC of the h3c,nx30pro board from the
pdt_data_1 partition and derives the LAN MAC from it. The 112M partition
contract of this device has no pdt_data_1 partition, because that space is
part of the larger UBI area. On this layout the base therefore finds no
MAC at all.

Take the WAN MAC from a provisioned file first, then from the factory data
area, and only then from the stock partition when it is still present. The
provisioned file is not part of the image: it is written at deployment time
from the MAC of the stock device.

When no MAC is found the interface keeps the address the bootloader handed
over instead of getting a wrong one, and the factory write only happens
when a real WAN MAC was found.

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network b/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
index 7ee5472..4ec3760 100755
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -183,11 +183,30 @@ mediatek_setup_macs()
 		label_mac=$lan_mac
 		;;
 	h3c,nx30pro)
-		wan_mac=$(mtd_get_mac_ascii pdt_data_1 ethaddr)
-		lan_mac=$(macaddr_add $wan_mac 1)
-		if [ "$(mtk_factory_get_byte "Factory" 4 2)" = "00-0c" ]; then
-			local wifi_mac="$(macaddr_add $wan_mac 2)"
-			mtk_facrory_write_mac "Factory" 4 $wifi_mac
+		# The 112M partition contract has no pdt_data_1 partition, so the
+		# stock location of the WAN MAC is gone on this layout. Take the MAC
+		# from a provisioned file first, then from the factory data area, and
+		# only then from the stock partition when it is still there. The
+		# provisioned file is written at deployment time and is not part of
+		# the image.
+		if [ -f /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac ]; then
+			wan_mac="$(cat /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac)"
+		fi
+		if [ -z "$wan_mac" ]; then
+			wan_mac=$(mtd_get_mac_ascii Factory ethaddr)
+		fi
+		if [ -z "$wan_mac" ]; then
+			wan_mac=$(mtd_get_mac_ascii pdt_data_1 ethaddr)
+		fi
+		if [ -n "$wan_mac" ]; then
+			lan_mac=$(macaddr_add $wan_mac 1)
+			if [ "$(mtk_factory_get_byte "Factory" 4 2)" = "00-0c" ]; then
+				local wifi_mac="$(macaddr_add $wan_mac 2)"
+				mtk_facrory_write_mac "Factory" 4 $wifi_mac
+			fi
+		else
+			logger -t board.d -p user.warn \
+				"No WAN MAC found for h3c,nx30pro, provision /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac"
 		fi
 		;;
 	*clt,r30b1* |\
